[[:db/retract 17592186152825 :question/answer-fields 17592186151427] {:db/id 17592186152202 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-58fa3eda-7303-530c-b266-fd43b4b16a9f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152825 :question/problem "![](images/9d/9df0c9dd8b76ac337b6110fc92019924ad2ee1c4cc0da8216c27709b641a8451.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\n- $f(-2)\\ne f(0)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is **one-to-one**" :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the graph, we have $f(-2)=f(0)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Again, we have $f(-2)=f(0)$ but $-2\\ne 0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since statement II is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-67bb5409-539d-5019-8102-b7a8fb7859d7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-67bb5409-539d-5019-8102-b7a8fb7859d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "67bb5409-539d-5019-8102-b7a8fb7859d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8adf8b3d-ac7a-52cf-8b4c-03f7c2608d36" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9d38aa51-050c-524f-9c39-3aa01c15091e" "answer-dae716d0-1847-54c9-9892-a356fbf81aea" "answer-e4388827-d9f0-5814-8367-e64cdc9001a1" "answer-02c08a79-bba6-544e-a9ea-ca58b06c0451" "answer-8adf8b3d-ac7a-52cf-8b4c-03f7c2608d36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d38aa51-050c-524f-9c39-3aa01c15091e" :answer/id #uuid "9d38aa51-050c-524f-9c39-3aa01c15091e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dae716d0-1847-54c9-9892-a356fbf81aea" :answer/id #uuid "dae716d0-1847-54c9-9892-a356fbf81aea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4388827-d9f0-5814-8367-e64cdc9001a1" :answer/id #uuid "e4388827-d9f0-5814-8367-e64cdc9001a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02c08a79-bba6-544e-a9ea-ca58b06c0451" :answer/id #uuid "02c08a79-bba6-544e-a9ea-ca58b06c0451" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8adf8b3d-ac7a-52cf-8b4c-03f7c2608d36" :answer/id #uuid "8adf8b3d-ac7a-52cf-8b4c-03f7c2608d36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-58fa3eda-7303-530c-b266-fd43b4b16a9f" :question/id #uuid "58fa3eda-7303-530c-b266-fd43b4b16a9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80370" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c2f22af3b39c28d885ac490aae190e1b2d4ad55828a552fec031069d6d912a2.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\n- $f(0)=f(1)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is **one-to-one**" :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the graph, we have $f(0)=0$ and $f(1)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $R$ that map to the same element in $R.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dff19999-9a3e-55e9-8a46-2ed82f902f83"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dff19999-9a3e-55e9-8a46-2ed82f902f83" :answer-field/id #uuid "dff19999-9a3e-55e9-8a46-2ed82f902f83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bbe41323-bdcb-5854-b702-4569e847d444" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5ef0e88-3d5a-58fe-a094-21c1a2d940b0" "answer-486699da-5c52-50b7-a5e8-06a33ea08707" "answer-bbe41323-bdcb-5854-b702-4569e847d444" "answer-21c583e6-ea60-5d7f-b515-6a1c05522f68" "answer-d388ffe7-607b-5621-9d65-a25de45df1c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5ef0e88-3d5a-58fe-a094-21c1a2d940b0" :answer/id #uuid "c5ef0e88-3d5a-58fe-a094-21c1a2d940b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-486699da-5c52-50b7-a5e8-06a33ea08707" :answer/id #uuid "486699da-5c52-50b7-a5e8-06a33ea08707" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbe41323-bdcb-5854-b702-4569e847d444" :answer/id #uuid "bbe41323-bdcb-5854-b702-4569e847d444" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21c583e6-ea60-5d7f-b515-6a1c05522f68" :answer/id #uuid "21c583e6-ea60-5d7f-b5