swer-field-9e246480-5cbb-5dda-adb1-b0ac60280c69" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e246480-5cbb-5dda-adb1-b0ac60280c69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8a08c9ad-68d3-5048-9aa1-f2e7ffb89cb5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8a08c9ad-68d3-5048-9aa1-f2e7ffb89cb5" "answer-036d9afb-4836-58e3-9109-9dd285d1e857" "answer-4a28a6ba-2618-5929-9239-4e604586dd15" "answer-8affdd3e-63cb-5945-abff-fdb11ff377f3" "answer-3c173147-60ba-5870-bce4-c2f5db134f39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a08c9ad-68d3-5048-9aa1-f2e7ffb89cb5" :answer/id #uuid "8a08c9ad-68d3-5048-9aa1-f2e7ffb89cb5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-036d9afb-4836-58e3-9109-9dd285d1e857" :answer/id #uuid "036d9afb-4836-58e3-9109-9dd285d1e857" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a28a6ba-2618-5929-9239-4e604586dd15" :answer/id #uuid "4a28a6ba-2618-5929-9239-4e604586dd15" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8affdd3e-63cb-5945-abff-fdb11ff377f3" :answer/id #uuid "8affdd3e-63cb-5945-abff-fdb11ff377f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c173147-60ba-5870-bce4-c2f5db134f39" :answer/id #uuid "3c173147-60ba-5870-bce4-c2f5db134f39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1a3dbd42-cd16-5083-8842-33f0028feb3d" :question/id #uuid "1a3dbd42-cd16-5083-8842-33f0028feb3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105207" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,4]\\to [-3,9]$ which is given by $f(x)=2x+1?$\n\n- $f(-2)=f(4)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is an injection" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/5f/5fd931a87d6a5fb32d10ed931f443a8175f0760eba9fe2fe69336f8f79e9fd68.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have $f(2)=2(-2)+1=-3$ and $f(4)=2\\cdot 4+1=9.$\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $[-2,4]$ that map to the same element in $[-3,9].$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,4],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6472838c-210f-5ad0-99a2-67a0bbd5ad6b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6472838c-210f-5ad0-99a2-67a0bbd5ad6b" :answer-field/id #uuid "6472838c-210f-5ad0-99a2-67a0bbd5ad6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9b94f507-0ee4-574c-849e-434a6fd9142d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-76f0dd4e-ff74-50db-9f41-52a58331f2e9" "answer-3d4e93b6-1460-51b3-854b-d70d0185543b" "answer-9b94f507-0ee4-574c-849e-434a6fd9142d" "answer-5f61eda3-2ef3-5e67-a98c-6effd83ff8d6" "answer-27143f05-01a0-516c-bb47-d27121720b6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76f0dd4e-ff74-50db-9f41-52a58331f2e9" :answer/id #uuid "76f0dd4e-ff74-50db-9f41-52a58331f2e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d4e93b6-1460-51b3-854b-d70d0185543b" :answer/id #uuid "3d4e93b6-1460-51b3-854b-d70d0185543b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b94f507-0ee4-574c-849e-434a6fd9142d" :answer/id #uuid "9b94f507-0ee4-574c-849e-434a6fd9142d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f61eda3-2ef3-5e67-a98c-6effd83ff8d6" :answer/id #uuid "5f61eda3-2ef3-5e67-a98c-6effd83ff8d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27143f05-01a0-516c-bb47-d27121720b6d" :answer/id #uuid "27143f05-01a0-516c-bb47-d27121720b6d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152201 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-23e55f80-c083-57f4-820d-7aa2d67256ab"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-23e55f80-c083-57f4-820d-7aa2d67256ab" :question/id #uuid "23e55f80-c083-57f4-820d-7aa2d67256ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-105210" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n\n- $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=2x+3$\n- $g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=(x-2)^{2}$\n- $h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- I is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3 & =2{x}_{2}+3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- II is *not*  an injection.  For example, $g(1)=1=g(3),$ but $1\\ne 3.$\n\n- III is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(2\\pi ),$ but $0\\ne 2\\pi .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-50962eb5-13e0-5527-99de-391f22e7ee03"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-50962eb5-13e0-5527-99de-391f22e7ee03" :answer-field/id #uuid "50962eb5-13e0-5527-99de-391f22e7ee03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-60027804-dbc8-5ba3-b7bd-f44642116bde" :answer-field/choices ["answer-34cfe54f-4c1a-5601-9bd2-0f1892a607c6" "answer-60027804-dbc8-5ba3-b7bd-f44642116bde" "answer-ad5fab01-32db-5160-9eaf-32f4b30665c5" "answer-8c1d872d-1050-528d-989c-6e743504ef10" "answer-965d76be-2ba3-58ed-b51e-9ca0ad934ed0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34cfe54f-4c1a-5601-9bd2-0f1892a607c6" :answer/id #uuid "34cfe54f-4c1a-5601-9bd2-0f1892a607c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60027804-dbc8-5ba3-b7bd-f44642116bde" :answer/id #uuid "60027804-dbc8-5ba3-b7bd-f44642116bde" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad5fab01-32db-5160-9eaf-32f4b30665c5" :answer/id #uuid "ad5fab01-32db-5160-9eaf-32f4b30665c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c1d872d-1050-528d-989c-6e743504ef10" :answer/id #uuid "8c1d872d-1050-528d-989c-6e743504ef10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-965d76be-2ba3-58ed-b51e-9ca0ad934ed0" :answer/id #uuid "965d76be-2ba3-58ed-b51e-9ca0ad934ed0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3676bd2b-76e7-5096-8724-d2aba2e73baf" :activity/id #uuid "3676bd2b-76e7-5096-8724-d2aba2e73baf" :activity/title "Injections" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051041 :activity/course 17592186046679 :activity/steps ["step-d93d6add-1d7b-59c0-9993-38adf9231b4c" "step-2530907e-f808-5c7f-87ec-10398577b7b1" "step-59126e0e-e63f-5afb-b7f9-f